INT. ALPINE CABLE CAR - DAY

A glass cabin hangs mid-span between two peaks, swaying in the wind. Snow-ridged valley two thousand feet below. The machinery has stopped.

INSPECTOR BALTHAZAR GREY, 50s, long grey coat, folds his hands over a silver-topped cane.

MADAME SOLANGE VEIL, 60s, in sable and diamonds, clutches a jewelled handbag.

COLONEL RUPERT ASHBY, 70s, ramrod straight, medals pinned to his lapel, glares through the window.

MISS PENELOPE DRAKE, 20s, a nurse in a blue cape, sits on the bench with her knees together.

MR. KASIMIR NOVAK, 40s, in a cheap brown suit, sweats and stares at his shoes.

They all turn at once. Grey knocks his cane against the floor. Everyone else freezes.

GREY
Ladies and gentlemen, I shall be brief. Someone in this cabin killed Lord Pemberton last night.

ASHBY
Preposterous.

GREY
His body was found in the funicular station with a needle in his neck.

PENELOPE
Oh!

GREY
Miss Drake, you are the only person here trained to use a hypodermic.

PENELOPE
I'm a nurse, not an assassin!

GREY
Of course. But you were on his floor.

VEIL
So was I, Inspector. So was the Colonel.

ASHBY
Madame, I take exception.

VEIL
Take it, then. I saw you in the corridor at midnight.

ASHBY
I was returning from the smoking room.

VEIL
In your dressing gown?

ASHBY
It's cold!

GREY
Mr. Novak?

NOVAK
I was in my room. All night.

GREY
Then you will not mind if I search your jacket.

NOVAK
I will!

GREY
Why?

NOVAK
Because there is a letter in it.

GREY
From whom?

NOVAK
From the dead man.

The cabin sways. No one speaks. Wind whistles through the cables.

GREY
Read it aloud, Mr. Novak.

Novak draws out an envelope with trembling fingers. He opens it. His eyes move. His lips whiten.

NOVAK
"Whoever finds this, forgive me. I have taken my own life, and I wish it understood that no person is to blame."

PENELOPE
Suicide?

GREY
No, Miss Drake. A man who writes his own suicide note does not first poison himself with a needle in the neck.

ASHBY
Then the letter is forged.

GREY
The letter is genuine. And that is the interesting thing.

VEIL
Why?

GREY
Because the handwriting is Mr. Novak's.
